  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "How to use: https://github.com/pableess/Bleess.Extensions.Logging.File\n\n      Breaking changes in 4.0:\n      - Targets .NET 8, .NET 10 and .NET 11 (net6.0 and net9.0 were dropped, both are out of support)\n      - FileLoggerProvider takes a TimeProvider; AddFile/AddFiles register TimeProvider.System if none is registered\n      - File logger options are validated on startup (Path, MaxNumberFiles, MaxFileSizeInMB, MaxFlushInterval)\n      - Date based rolling can use UTC via FileLoggerOptions.UseUtcTimestamp\n\n      Fixes:\n      - Configuration changes now reload the file provider options (path, limits, formatter, flush settings)\n      - Composite logger IsEnabled reports enabled when any sub logger is enabled\n      - WithFilter(Func<string?, LogLevel, bool>) no longer ignores the predicate\n      - WithFormatter uses the formatter name it was given and applies formatter options to the sub provider\n      - Writer swaps no longer race with the write thread; the write thread owns the writer lifecycle",
